 "- **Forward propagation** — Pushing inputs through the layers to get predictions. The easy direction — and the one you must be able to do by hand before backprop means anything.",
 "- **Universal approximation** — A wide-enough single hidden layer can approximate continuous functions. Existence, not practicality: it says nothing about learnability, data, or generalization.",
 "- **Depth vs width** — Depth builds hierarchical features efficiently; width adds capacity per level. Deep-and-narrow usually beats shallow-and-wide for structured data.",
